{"engine":"Windows.Media.Ocr en-US","scale":3,"pages":[{"page":1,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"O","x":536,"y":272,"w":23,"h":23},{"text":"OFFICE OF","x":611,"y":167,"w":253,"h":37},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-","x":609,"y":233,"w":700,"h":48},{"text":"RECORDER & ELECTIONS","x":611,"y":309,"w":618,"h":50},{"text":"COUNTY OF SAN MATEO","x":611,"y":388,"w":569,"h":38},{"text":"RECEIVED","x":1486,"y":102,"w":301,"h":50},{"text":"AUG 1 1 CHURCH","x":1509,"y":196,"w":588,"h":71},{"text":"ELE TIONS OFFICER &","x":1763,"y":283,"w":398,"h":35},{"text":"TY CLERK-RECORDER","x":1861,"y":331,"w":379,"h":36},{"text":"Ballot Measure Rebuttal Argument Submission Form","x":550,"y":518,"w":1394,"h":54},{"text":"If both an argument in favor of and an argument against a measure have been selected for publication in the Sample","x":208,"y":601,"w":2053,"h":41},{"text":"Ballot & Official Voter Information Pamphlet, a typed rebuttal to the argument in favor of or the argument against the","x":207,"y":647,"w":2045,"h":41},{"text":"measure may be submitted as outlined in this form.","x":207,"y":694,"w":901,"h":42},{"text":"The author(s) of the primary argument of the measure may prepare and submit a rebuttal argument or may authorize","x":206,"y":771,"w":2055,"h":40},{"text":"in writing any other person or persons to prepare, submit or sign the rebuttal argument.","x":207,"y":817,"w":1528,"h":41},{"text":"A rebuttal argument will not be accepted unless accompanied by this completed form, which shall contain the printed","x":205,"y":893,"w":2053,"h":42},{"text":"name(s) and signature(s) of the person(s) submitting it or, if submitted on behalf of a bona fide association of citizens,","x":207,"y":939,"w":2064,"h":42},{"text":"the name of the association and the printed name and signature of at least one of its principal officers. Please make","x":205,"y":985,"w":2056,"h":42},{"text":"sure you are using proper format before submitting to the Elections Office.","x":205,"y":1031,"w":1416,"h":42},{"text":"Word count limit for Rebuttal Arguments = 250 words","x":205,"y":1110,"w":936,"h":41},{"text":"for the","x":842,"y":1188,"w":113,"h":32},{"text":"Ballot Measure","x":205,"y":1189,"w":264,"h":34},{"text":"Rebuttal to Argument in Favor of Measure","x":275,"y":1273,"w":739,"h":41},{"text":"ÄRebuttal to Argument Against Measure I","x":1291,"y":1253,"w":870,"h":76},{"text":"Signed by Same Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the Primary Argument","x":227,"y":1388,"w":1890,"h":41},{"text":"If the rebuttal argument is signed by the same individual(s) as those already selected for the Voter Information","x":229,"y":1484,"w":1931,"h":43},{"text":"Pamphlet for the primary argument, check the following box and skip the back side of this form.","x":228,"y":1531,"w":1678,"h":42},{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Is Signed by Same Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the","x":351,"y":1600,"w":1812,"h":43},{"text":"Primary Argument","x":350,"y":1650,"w":322,"h":39},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":350,"y":1708,"w":566,"h":33},{"text":"Phone:","x":350,"y":1855,"w":123,"h":30},{"text":"Email:","x":1249,"y":1853,"w":105,"h":32},{"text":"Signed by Different Individual(s) than Individual(s) Selected for the Voter Information Pamphlet for the","x":226,"y":2008,"w":1928,"h":43},{"text":"Primary Argument","x":227,"y":2059,"w":346,"h":38},{"text":"The author(s) of the primary argument may authorize any other person or persons to sign the rebuttal argument. If","x":224,"y":2123,"w":2020,"h":42},{"text":"signers are new for the rebuttal argument, please check the following box, complete the back side of this form and","x":224,"y":2168,"w":2005,"h":43},{"text":"attach the written authorization (the Authorization Form for Change in Signers of Rebuttal Argument) from the","x":225,"y":2215,"w":1922,"h":42},{"text":"primary argument author(s).","x":225,"y":2264,"w":489,"h":40},{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Is Signed by New Signers as Authorized by Primary Argument Author(s)","x":348,"y":2339,"w":1612,"h":43},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":348,"y":2410,"w":566,"h":33},{"text":"P2AKu—","x":829,"y":2475,"w":208,"h":71},{"text":"Phone:","x":348,"y":2558,"w":123,"h":31},{"text":"Email:","x":1246,"y":2556,"w":105,"h":31},{"text":"Arguments will be emailed to the contact person listed here for review before they are printed in the Sample","x":218,"y":2725,"w":2041,"h":44},{"text":"Ballot & Official Voter Information Pamphlets,","x":809,"y":2772,"w":860,"h":39},{"text":"Please complete the reverse side of this form.","x":808,"y":2841,"w":865,"h":41},{"text":"40 Tower Road, San Mateo, CA 94402","x":866,"y":2898,"w":745,"h":41},{"text":"P 650.312.5222 F 650.312.5348 email registrar@smcacre.gov web www.smcacre.gov","x":384,"y":2951,"w":1713,"h":43}]},{"page":2,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"It's undeniable - severe Caltrain and BART station closures and service cuts would","x":293,"y":318,"w":1739,"h":41},{"text":"affect all San Mateo County residents - worsening traffic and straining transportation","x":290,"y":382,"w":1771,"h":47},{"text":"options for hundreds of thousands of Bay Area residents who need to get to work or","x":289,"y":446,"w":1768,"h":46},{"text":"medical appointments.","x":291,"y":511,"w":472,"h":44},{"text":"Please consider the FACTS and don't be misled by half-truths and exaggerations:","x":291,"y":619,"w":1717,"h":47},{"text":"FACT: Before supporting the Regional Transit Measure, business groups and local","x":290,"y":714,"w":1732,"h":48},{"text":"leaders ensured the measure included strong accountability and oversight requirements","x":289,"y":779,"w":1851,"h":46},{"text":"- BART and other large agencies must show cost savings to continue to receive","x":287,"y":842,"w":1678,"h":47},{"text":"dedicated operating funding.","x":287,"y":906,"w":599,"h":46},{"text":"FACT: Based on detailed financial analysis and projections, Caltrain and BART found","x":289,"y":999,"w":1790,"h":48},{"text":"that without the Regional Transit Measure, Caltrain could close up to one-third of","x":286,"y":1063,"w":1703,"h":47},{"text":"stations, drastically reduce frequency, and stop late night and weekend service entirely.","x":287,"y":1125,"w":1837,"h":49},{"text":"BART could cut service by 70% and close 15 stations including Colma, San Bruno,","x":288,"y":1189,"w":1743,"h":48},{"text":"South San Francisco, and Millbrae. These cuts would disrupt daily life and push","x":287,"y":1253,"w":1677,"h":46},{"text":"thousands more cars onto Highways 101, 280, 92, and local streets","x":286,"y":1317,"w":1423,"h":47},{"text":"FACT: taxpayers from across San Mateo County support the Regional Transit Measure,","x":301,"y":1410,"w":1841,"h":49},{"text":"along with stakeholders who don't always agree- business, labor, environmental, and","x":286,"y":1474,"w":1790,"h":48},{"text":"community groups,","x":286,"y":1540,"w":398,"h":46},{"text":"FACT: Without this measure, commutes would be longer and more unpredictable as","x":288,"y":1633,"w":1764,"h":47},{"text":"people who depend on transit are forced onto already-crowded streets, roads and","x":287,"y":1696,"w":1718,"h":48},{"text":"highways.","x":287,"y":1764,"w":204,"h":44},{"text":"FACT: The Regional Transit Measure invests money directly into San Mateo County","x":288,"y":1855,"w":1763,"h":49},{"text":"communities, providing funding for transit improvements and road repaving.","x":286,"y":1920,"w":1589,"h":47},{"text":"FACT: Don't be misled- Regional Transit Measure does NOT tax rent, utilities,","x":287,"y":2015,"w":1629,"h":47},{"text":"prescription medicines, or most groceries.","x":287,"y":2080,"w":879,"h":47},{"text":"VOTE YES ON RTM to preserve our Bay Area quality of life for future generations -","x":283,"y":2174,"w":1759,"h":47},{"text":"www.connectbayarea.com","x":283,"y":2240,"w":556,"h":45}]},{"page":3,"width":2436,"height":3156,"lines":[{"text":"Rebuttal Argument Signers 